course: dictionary
lesson: 2643
title: Detection
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Detection means noticing or finding something that is hard to see, hear or find. «Detection dogs are trained to sniff out things such as drugs, explosives, fruit carried in bags, money and even some illnesses.» The dogs find hidden things by smell, so detection here means finding.
explain: Detection can also mean finding out who did a crime or how it was done. That is detective work. In a story, the detective uses clues to work out what happened. The context tells you which meaning fits.
explain: In science, detection means using instruments to find and measure something. «Collision detection is the game checking every frame whether two hitboxes (invisible shapes around things) overlap; if the player overlaps a wall, the game pushes the player back.» Here detection is a computer checking whether two things touch.
explain: To test a meaning, put it into the sentence in place of the hard word. If "finding" still makes sense, you are probably right. A smoke alarm gives early detection of a fire, which saves lives.
fact: Detection is a noun, so it names an action or a process.
fact: «Early detection» means finding something at the start, before it gets worse.
fact: «Avoid detection» means staying unnoticed, and «escape detection» means getting away without being found.
fact: «Smoke detection» means finding smoke, often with an alarm.
fact: Detection is mostly uncountable, so you usually say «detection» without «a» or plural forms.
exercise: «Detection dogs are trained to sniff out things such as drugs, explosives, fruit carried in bags, money and even some illnesses.» What is a detection dog's job? | Running races in the park | *Finding hidden things by smell | Carrying heavy shopping | Guarding the house from the sun
exercise: Which phrase means staying unnoticed? | early detection | smoke detection | metal detection | *avoid detection
exercise: In a game, what does collision detection check? | *Whether two objects overlap | How many points the player has | The colour of the sky | The name of the player
test: Why is early detection of a fire by a smoke alarm helpful? | It stops the alarm from ringing | *It warns people while there is still time to get out | It means the fire has already gone out | It makes the fire bigger
test: In a story, what is detection? | Cooking a meal | Playing a musical instrument | *Finding out who did a crime or how it was done | Growing a plant
exam: A scientist uses a detector to find traces of metal in the soil. What does detection mean here? | Painting the detector red | *Using instruments to find and measure something | Telling a joke to the soil | Digging a hole for a plant
